summary:
  Five minutes on, the move is written without asking whether the old address
  answers again.

history:
  The wait alone proves nothing: the listener was on the new address the whole
  time and nobody looked at the old one. The second look opens it, and an
  address that plays again keeps its place in the list.

target:
  package/contents/ui/HealLogic.js

find:
      if (aliveAnswer(status, contentType)) return "keep";

replace:
      if (false) return "keep";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_heallogic.qml::test_the_second_look_keeps_a_living_address_and_moves_a_gone_one.
  Line-neutral.
